AB  - This paper presents a three-stage passwordless multi-factor authentication framework specifically designed for digital wallet applications operating on permissioned blockchain networks. The proposed system addresses critical security vulnerabilities inherent in traditional password-based authentication mechanisms by integrating device identity verification,validator-based access control under IBFT 2.0 consensus, and cryptographic validation [24]. Through a novel three-stage authentication protocol, the framework eliminates dependency on memorized credentials while maintaining regulatory compliance and auditability requirements essential for financial applications. Experimental results demonstrate a 99.8% authentication success rate with zero successful brute-force attacks in over 1,000,000 simulated attempts. The system reduces transaction authentication latency by 47% compared to conventional multi-factor approaches while maintaining full compliance with financial industry security standards. This research contributes to the evolving landscape of blockchain security and authentication mechanisms in fintech applications. Β©2025 IEEE.
