AB  - The centralized control systems transition into the data driven technologies has intensified concerns over privacy, security and centralized control. The federated learning (FL) with blockchain act as revolutionary paradigm to address the problems of centralized control technologies. The big shift is done to address challenge towards privacy preservation and secure collaborative intelligence. In FL, multiple participants are allowed to train machine learning models without transferring their data to maintain the privacy risks. FL faces various challenges in trust, incentive calculation and identification of malicious actors. On the other hand, Blockchain is a decentralized in nature and having cryptographic security. Smart contracts enhance the capabilities of blockchain is to ensure transparency, immutability and coordination among participants. In this chapter comprehensive view is provided for integration of FL with blockchain. The integration exploits the finest features of both and provides the comprehensive view. The features of both technologies i.e., FL and blockchain are discussed. The integration of both technologies strengthens the privacy, security and incentive calculation mechanisms. The cryptographic techniques are discussed for the optimized dynamic federated learning environment. In this chapter the future advancements in building scalable, secure and trustless FL and blockchain ecosystems is shown. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Swati Sah, Rejwan Bin Sulaieman, and Aditya Dayal Tyagi; individual chapters, the contributors.
