AB  - The integration of the Internet of Things (IoT) into healthcare systems has enhanced capabilities for real-time monitoring and data -driven personalized treatment. However, the massive volume of sensitive data generated by IoT devices introduces serious security and privacy challenges. Conventional security models are ill-equipped to address the decentralized and resource-constrained nature of IoT environments. This paper proposes a blockchain-based security framework for 10T-enabled healthcare, which ensures tamper-evident data recording, decentralized access control, and cryptographic integrity validation. The proposed model utilizes encryption, digital signatures, and smart contracts deployed on a permissioned Ethereum blockchain. A five-layer architecture, including IoT sensing, se-cure gateway, blockchain ledger, smart contract enforcement, and user interface, is designed and formalized. Simulated experiments demonstrate robust performance in latency, throughput, and attack resistance. Our model outperforms traditional centralized approaches in scalability, integrity assurance, and dynamic access control. The results validate the potential of blockchain-integrated IoT frameworks in building secure, scalable, and auditable diaital healthcare infrastructures. Β© 2025 IEEE.
