AB  - Border conflicts such as those between India and Pakistan often result in severe disruptions to civilian communication systems. Ensuring secure, real-time, and tamper-proof communication is critical for coordinating relief, issuing alerts, and maintaining public safety. This paper proposes a cryptographic framework designed specifically for secure civilian communication during conflict scenarios. The framework integrates lightweight encryption algorithms, decentralized identity management, and blockchain-based logging to ensure confi-dentiality, integrity, and authenticity of messages exchanged through mobile and IoT devices. We evaluate the framework on parameters such as encryption latency, resilience to interception, and adaptability to low-connectivity environments. Experimental results demonstrate the viability of the system in delivering secure communication under constrained network conditions while preserving privacy and auditability.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
