AB  - The growing complexity of the multi-layered Internet infrastructure eco-systems e.g. smart cities, industrial IoT networks, and extended reality ecosystems requires evolutionary intelligent and adaptive cybersecurity frameworks with the real-time threat mitigation capabilities. This paper is going to present a new Meta-Cognitive Swarm Intelligencedriven Cyber Defense Architecture (MCSI-CDA) that brings well-coordinated meta-cognitive learning, swarm intelligence, and zero-trust enforcement to autonomously and proactively provide planless and continuous cyber defense. Its architecture features Meta-Cognitive Learning Engine (MCLE) which can self-regulate the detection strategies on the basis of uncertainty in the environmental situation and past performance. Considering the idea of how resilience and fault tolerance can be achieved, a Swarm Intelligence Coordination Layer (SICL) can offer decentralized anomaly consensus based on bioinspired optimization algorithms. The Zero-Trust Policy Enforcer (ZTPE) provides stringent access control and blockchain-based auditability with the Multi-Layered Threat Perception Module (MTPM) tracing contextual anomalies through graph neural networks across the physical, cyber and application layers. Moreover, a Quantum-Resilient Cryptographic Unit (QRCU), protecting communication channels against quantum-powered adversaries in the future, is also in use. Collectively these will constitute a single, selfadaptive security infrastructure with the ability to learn, grow and react in milliseconds. The suggested MCSI-CDA framework is an important advance on the way to the development of intelligent, real-time, and scalable cybersecurity solutions applied to the next generations of hyper-connected digital frameworks. The suggested MCSI-CDA approach has an overall accuracy of 97.8%. Β© 2025 IEEE.
