AB  - Blockchain and ML offer a potential way out of some of the biggest challenges to date with data provenance, security and decentralization. It therefore becomes increasingly relevant to preserve the integrity, traceability and privacy of data since ML algorithms are increasingly used to make and influence decisions within healthcare, the Internet of Things (IoT), finance and even in supply chains. Blockchain technology can provide a transparent, non-alterable ledger to enable a safe data sharing to train collaborative models, safely losing sensitive data. The survey explores basic framework and methods including federated learning, smart contracts, cryptographic improvements, and consensus algorithms, that underpin the union of blockchain and ML. In addition, it also explores some practical applications, uncovers the issues, including scalability, latency, and compliance with regulations, and proposes future development directions, aiming at the construction of lightweight, privacy-preserving, and interoperable systems. The results highlight the radical capabilities of blockchain to create reliable and stable ML systems concurrently with overcoming the current deficiencies of the technology. Β© 2025 IEEE.
