AB  - Managing and maintaining school records has long posed a challenge due to the need for a secure system that ensures the transparency and reliability of institutional results. Blockchain is a promising technology that can offer a solution to this challenge. It enables decentralized and transactional data sharing among a large network of untrusted participants without relying on a central integration point that all components in the system must trust. In this chapter, we propose a Blockchain-based storage system for school records and grades that uses a combination of Blockchain, storage servers and cryptography techniques to create a secure and reliable environment. We also explore the use of Blockchain as a Service to implement distributed database systems. Our proposed solution uses the SHA256 algorithm for security, a cryptographic hash that generates a unique 256-number signature for an information document. This algorithm is also used for password verification, as it allows for the verification of correct passwords without actually storing them. Our proposal employs smart contracts to regulate the process of storage and sharing, making it more secure and reliable than current solutions. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Nazmul Siddique, Mohammad Shamsul Arefin, Sheak Rashed Haider Noori, and M Shamim Kaiser; individual chapters, the contributors.
