AB  - Intelligent healthcare intends to provide a platform to remotely monitor usersβ€™ health-related data based on wearable devices as the Internet of Things (IoT) develops. The development of blockchain and AI technologies also supports the advancement of secure, intelligent healthcare. Data is still susceptible to attack and privacy leaks because they are kept on a cloud server. In order to ensure patient safety and privacy when utilizing medical equipment, patient information, such as health status, must be protected. Experts securely exchange information about healthcare in order to analyze healthcare and give patients timely care. Deep Learning (DL) algorithms and other recent cryptographic and biometric systems have been widely employed to authenticate and detect abnormalities in order to ensure protection for healthcare systems. Since the gridβ€™s sensors are energy-constrained procedures, a security mechanism based on DL techniques has been implemented. Security and efficiency must be balanced. In order to protect data transmission from exterior extortions with minimal encryption and decryption time, a novel framework known as deep Q-learning based neural network with privacy preservation technique (DQ-NNPP) was developed in this work. Comparatively, the suggested model performed better than various conventional methods. Parametric analysis has been carried out in terms of accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, communication overhead, encryption time, and decryption time. Β© 2025 Apple Academic Press, Inc.
