AB  - This paper addresses the critical challenge of enforcing mandatory data access control within the Trusted Energy Data Space (TEDS) infrastructure. The authors propose a cryptographic solution combining Attribute-Based Proxy ReEncryption (AB-PRE) with blockchain technology to secure data sharing against potential threats, including honest-but-curious service platform and single-point failures. The core innovation is a framework that enables fine-grained, policy-based data encryption while allowing authorized proxy nodes to transform ciphertexts for legitimate users without accessing plaintext. This approach ensures that energy data-which reflects both corporate operations and personal behaviors-remains protected throughout its lifecycle within the TEDS ecosystem. Security analysis demonstrates collusion-resistant data protection and nonrepudiable auditability through blockchain-integrated logging. Experimental implementation confirms practical efficiency, with encryption, re-encryption, and decryption operations completing within 1.5-5.2 seconds. This work provides a standardized, scalable solution for privacy-preserving data flow in trusted energy data space, aligning with China's evolving data governance policies while maintaining good performance suitable for realworld deployment. Β© 2025 IEEE.
