AB  - Blockchain (BC) technology can revolutionize decentralized supply chain management and healthcare system administration. The study examines how blockchain technology might increase productivity, security, and transparency in several fields. Blockchain technology can create an immutable database for commodity tracking, reduce fraud, and enable trustless stakeholder cooperation in supply chain management. It provides real-time accountability and traceability. Blockchain technology enables interoperable EHRs, efficient pharmaceutical supply chains, and safe patient data interchange, improving patient outcomes and operational integrity. The research emphasizes blockchain's cryptographic security, smart contracts, and decentralized consensus mechanisms as crucial tools for solving present shortcomings and inefficiencies. Scalability issues, regulatory constraints, and significant implementation costs must be solved for wider adoption. Blockchain increases data security, reduces inefficiencies, and ensures worldwide standards in case studies and experiments. All evidence suggest blockchain has revolutionary potential, enabling new decentralized systems. This study will inform legislators and stakeholders that want to use blockchain technology to better healthcare and supply chain management. Β© 2025 IEEE.
