AB  - The challenges of multi-agency collaboration and evidence integrity are becoming more and more prevalent in digital forensic investigations. In order to create tamper-proof chain of custody records and facilitate safe inter-jurisdictional sharing, this paper presents a blockchain-based evidence management system. Our method automates the tracking and verification of evidence by combining forensic-specific smart contracts with permissioned blockchain networks. Experiments in three law enforcement scenarios show improved legal admissibility, 65% faster evidence processing, and the removal of documentation gaps. The system supports current forensic workflows while preserving the authenticity of cryptographic proof of evidence. The framework enables real-time tracking, evidence preservation, and interdisciplinary collaboration, providing law enforcement with scalable tools for proactive intervention. This study marks a paradigm shift in digital forensics, bridging technological innovation and investigative integrity to counter evolving cyber threats.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
