AB  - As financial technologies (FinTechs) and central bank digital currencies (CBDCs) become more common, it is more important than ever to protect data integrity, privacy, and non-repudiation. To solve these problems, we suggest FinTechSec++, a layered security framework that uses advanced cryptographic primitives, secure multi-party computation, and blockchain-anchored logs. FinTechSec++ protects data from the beginning to the end with little latency (β‰¤12 ms per transaction) and stops common attacks like replay, tampering, and insider compromise. It does this by using threat modeling and performance evaluation on a prototype implementation. We have made three contributions: (1) a new hybrid encryption signature scheme for data that is not being used and (2) a non-repudiation protocol that uses threshold signatures and timestamps. (3) an extensible architecture that can be used with existing FinTech/CBDC platforms. FinTechSec++ passes strict SBI compliance tests in both simulated and real-world situations, with a maximum throughput of 1,200 TPS. Β© 2025 IEEE.
