AB  - As electric vehicles (EVs) become more prevalent, ensuring secure and transparent tracking of their charging activities has emerged as a critical challenge. Traditional centralized methods are vulnerable to data integrity issues and lack resilience, raising concerns about trustworthiness. This work presents a blockchain-enhanced architecture for auditing EV charging sessions. It offloads Charging Data Records (CDRs) to the InterPlanetary File System (IPFS), while preserving their integrity through cryptographic anchors recorded on an Ethereum-compatible smart contract. This approach strikes a balance between decentralization and system performance. A prototype was developed featuring OCPP-based session simulation and automated verification via smart contracts. Experimental evaluation across thousands of test cases confirmed the system's ability to detect data tampering with minimal processing overhead, especially when integrated with Layer-2 scaling technologies. These results demonstrate the framework's potential to improve transparency and trust in EV charging networks. Β© 2025 IEEE.
