AB  - Blockchain technology has revolutionised data sharing and storage by offering decentralised, impenetrable solutions in a variety of fields. But because of its intrinsic transparency, there are serious privacy issues, especially when handling sensitive data. To improve information retrieval and protect user privacy in blockchain systems, this paper offers a thorough analysis of many cryptographic signature algorithms. It looks at the advantages and disadvantages of current strategies, highlights important obstacles, and talks about possible fixes to privacy issues. This paper also provides a comparative evaluation of related works according to criteria like security, scalability, and efficiency. The knowledge acquired aids in the creation of privacy-protecting techniques that maximise data retrieval in blockchain-based applications. Β© 2025 IEEE.
