AB  - To facilitate the intelligent and digital transformation of the power grid, Grid Corporations have undertaken the construction of a data center-oriented infrastructure. This architecture enables the real-time acquisition, analysis, and sharing of massive volumes of electricity data, thereby significantly enhancing the efficiency of grid dispatching and the utilization of energy resources. However, the existing power data-sharing systems suffer from a lack of comprehensive auditing mechanisms, giving rise to several critical risks-including difficulty in tracking access behaviors, opacity in data transmission processes, and challenges in tracing the source of data leakage. These issues collectively compromise the trustworthiness and operational stability of the overall system. In response to these concerns, this paper proposes a blockchain-based auditable data-sharing scheme, which integrates smart contracts and cryptographic primitives to implement decentralized access control and behavioral auditing. The proposed solution ensures not only secure and traceable data interactions but also maintains favorable performance and scalability, as validated through experimental evaluation.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
