AB  - In this chapter, we explore the intricacies of blockchain technology and its impact on the weaknesses of big tech. Transforming numerous industries but also posing new security challenges, blockchain has often claimed decentralization, immutability, and transparency as its pillars. We discuss the integration of blockchain by many large tech firms and highlight examples of its application in finance, supply chain, and data. I like how the chapter then dives into a more thorough discussion on vulnerabilities particular to the property left to blockchain, from 51% attacks to clear contract bugs to Sybil attacks-all while relying on case studies that are hands-down the best building complaints in the industry such as the DAO Hack and Poly Network Hack. Next, we talk about the transparent nature of blockchain harvesting and why some consider it a double-edged sword, as a technical advantage and a risk factor. Tech companies looking to build solutions should adopt multiple blockchain implementations but also begin with regular audits, cryptographic security, and robust smart contracts, and this regulation, however that happens, makes the world more conducive to real-world applications especially as the founding generation's attention turns elsewhere, we outline steps for robust security. This chapter ends with insights into the new trends and innovative developments in blockchain technology, the evolution of blockchain security over the coming years, and the significant impact big tech players will have on the future of blockchain technology. This chapter tackles all these pressing concerns, and in doing so, it frames the precarious balance between all the things blockchain has to offer and everything it could destroy to make big tech applications safe and reputable. Β© 2026 selection and editorial matter, Arun Kumar Singh, Sandeep Saxena and A.K. Haghi.
