AB  - Ransomware encrypts critical files using algorithms like AES and RSA, demanding payment for decryption. Investigators struggle to recover data without the original keys, as attackers often erase logs and conceal activity. Securing backups is essential to reduce damage. Forensic experts examine network traffic, memory dumps, and system logs to trace ransomware behavior. Tools like Wireshark and NetFlow detect unusual C2 connections. Evidence is preserved using file carving, hash analysis, and imaging. Ransom notes, IPs, and cryptographic signatures help identify attackers. Blockchain analysis tracks crypto payments, aided by law enforcement and exchanges. Understanding exploits and social engineering boosts defense. Β©2026, IGI Global Scientific Publishing. All rights reserved.
