AB  - Traditional financial transaction systems face significant challenges in ensuring trust, transparency, and security in distributed computing environments. Existing centralized architectures are vulnerable to single points of failure, data manipulation, and lack of auditability, necessitating innovative solutions to enhance trust mechanisms in applied computing systems for financial operations. This research proposes a novel blockchain-enabled secure framework that integrates cryptographic hashing, smart contracts, and consensus algorithms to establish immutable transaction records. The framework employs a hybrid consensus mechanism combining Proof-of-Authority and Byzantine Fault Tolerance protocols, implementing multi-layer encryption and real-time validation processes for financial transaction integrity. The proposed framework demonstrated 99.7% transaction accuracy, 98.5% fraud detection efficiency, and 96.8% system availability under stress testing conditions. Implementation results showed 85% reduction in transaction processing time and 92% improvement in audit trail transparency compared to conventional systems. The blockchain-enabled framework significantly enhances trust and confidence in financial reporting while enabling real-time transaction tracking, providing a robust foundation for secure financial computing systems with measurable improvements in accuracy, security, and operational efficiency. Β© 2026 IEEE.
