AB  - Ensuring secure and scalable storage for real-time data streams remains a challenge, especially in sectors that require auditability, such as finance and IoT. Although blockchain provides data integrity, full on-chain storage is costly and inefficient. To address this, we present a hybrid architecture that stores data off-chain while periodically anchoring cryptographic hashes on-chain using an interval-based batching approach. Our system allows for configurable batch sizes and intervals, balancing cost and security while ensuring data integrity. We implemented this architecture with modular components for data processing, off-chain storage, and blockchain anchoring. A cost analysis demonstrates the economic viability of our approach compared to fully on-chain solutions. Future work will focus on dynamic interval optimization, enhanced privacy mechanisms, and broader blockchain interoperability. Β© 2025 IEEE.
