AB  - With its 2008 introduction with Bitcoin, blockchain technology has quickly grown beyond cryptocurrencies to become a game-changing force in financial technology (Fintech). Financial institutions and tech entrepreneurs are showing a great deal of interest in blockchain since it uses decentralized, distributed ledger systems to improve financial transactions in terms of operational efficiency, transparency, data security, and efficiency. This paper studies blockchain's increasing role within Fintech, bringing out its current usage and future potential. Smart contracts, crowdfunding, Know Your Customer (KYC) procedures, and safe cross-border payments are important Fintech blockchain uses. Because blockchain technology is decentralized, it eliminates the need for middlemen, increasing transaction efficiency and reducing expenses. Additionally, blockchain facilitates real-time audits and improves security through cryptographic protocols, both of which are essential for sustaining digital banking and lowering the danger of fraud. Depending on the use case, the study also looks into the various types of blockchain networks, each of which has unique benefits. As technology continues to grow, its impact on Fintech and banking sector is also set to rise and increase, bringing out innovation and contributing to sustainability in financial and banking services. The future of blockchain technology in the financial sector is robust, except a few challenges it poses such as privacy, data protection and environmental impact which require important focus. The study concludes with the fact that blockchain will remain an anchor pillar in designing the future of digital finance, shifting economies towards better efficiency and bringing transparency and sustainability. Β© 2025 IEEE.
