AB  - The Internet of Things combined with blockchain technology has emerged as an innovative platform to better safeguard data, save costs, and pale, achieve strength. Combining blockchain and IoT means that the distributed ledger with sophisticated cryptographic mechanisms, consensus mechanisms, and some other processes may transmit data and information in a secure and open approach among devices across long distances. This paper begins with an introduction to the IoT and blockchain technology platforms before conducting a study of how their merger can help improve the platforms. The paper will additionally emphasize critical criteria before integrating the blockchain in IoT systems. Finally, the paper offers practical examples from blockchain-supported IoT project. Overall, combining blockchain technology into IoT might transform, how perceive and communicate technical advancements, paving the path for a more secure, connected, but decentralized future. Β© The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2025.
