AB  - Cloud storage users increasingly distribute their data across multiple providers such as Google Drive, Dropbox, One Drive, and AWS S3, leading to fragmented management, inconsistent access policies, and only having server side encryption. MyCloudControl is a unified multi-cloud management system that combines an Adaptive Encryption Engine, client-side zero-knowledge security, attribute based access control (ABAC), and blockchain based audit logging to address these challenges. All files are encrypted locally in the browser using dynamic cryptographic selection based on file sensitivity and user defined privacy levels, while a hierarchical key management scheme enables secure sharing via asymmetric key wrapping. A zero-knowledge blockchain ledger records pseudonymized access events without revealing file contents or identities and supports forensic analysis and compliance needs. Β© 2026 IEEE.
