AB  - Using blockchain technology, the Court Ledger modernizes and guarantees tamper-proof, transparent, distributed storage of court papers and forensic data, therefore securing judicial record-keeping. Whether manual or centralized, conventional techniques of preserving legal records are prone to mistakes, manipulation, and security lapses. This solution ensures the immutability of case files, court orders, and forensic evidence by including Ethereum-based smart contracts and cryptographic hashings, therefore allowing flawless, real-time access for approved legal practitioners. By use of permissionless blockchain architecture, the Court Ledger enhances the chain of custody for forensic evidence, therefore avoiding illegal changes and preserving the integrity of court processes. Along with improving data security, this creative solution simplifies case administration, therefore lowering administrative costs and building public confidence in the judicial system. Β© Grenze Scientific Society, 2025.
