AB  - The application of IoT devices in the healthcare sector has transformed remote patient monitoring and data harvesting, allowing for timely health assessments and tailored interventions. Nonetheless, the conventional IoT healthcare system's centralized framework poses major challenges with respect to privacy, security, and points of failure. This paper introduced the basic concept of forward a decentralized framework based on blockchain technology to enable secure and privacy-preserving sharing of data between healthcare IoT devices and stakeholders. The use of blockchain technology, including immutability, transparency, consensus protocols, and advanced cryptographic techniques achieves data integrity, patient privacy, and controlled restricted access without a central trusted authority. The framework provides sensitive medical data with scalable, secure, and resistant storage while allowing authorized users to access and share the data safely. Evaluations of the system's performance illustrate it's effective and resilient in actual healthcare settings, increasing trust and security while endorsing regulatory compliance within IoT frameworks.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
