AB  - This paper proposes an intelligent video surveillance system combining deep learning and blockchain technology for real-time violence detection in sensitive border areas of Senegal. The system integrates a hybrid architecture coupling MobileNetV2 for spatial feature extraction with LSTM networks for temporal behavioral analysis. Trained for 50 epochs on the Real-life Violence Situations dataset (2,000 videos), the model achieves 97.1% accuracy, 90.7% F1-score, and 85.1% recall. Real-time performance reaches 28-32 FPS on GPU and 15-18 FPS on CPU, demonstrating operational feasibility in resource-constrained environments. For evidence integrity, video files are stored on IPFS while cryptographic hashes are immutably registered on blockchain, ensuring tamper-proof verification and legal admissibility. Experimental validation confirms robust detection under diverse illumination and environmental conditions, paving the way toward legally compliant intelligent surveillance solutions for national security applications in West Africa.  Β© 2025 IEEE.
