AB  - Conventional vehicle monitoring systems have serious weaknesses. They face issues like a single point of failure, data tampering, and significant bandwidth problems from constant cloud streaming. This article introduces the Smart Vehicle Logging System (SVLS), a decentralized framework that uses Passive UHF RFID, Node.js-based edge computing, and blockchain technology. Unlike centralized systems that collect private recordings, this new design emphasizes data privacy through decentralized storage and edge-based processing. The system lowers the risks of centralizing large media files by keeping raw data at the network edge on Raspberry Pi nodes. To maintain data integrity and reduce duplication, only cryptographic SHA-256 hashes and metadata are permanently stored on a private blockchain ledger. A key innovation is the targeted retrieval mechanism, which uses fluent-ffmpeg to extract 60-second evidence clips only when authorized requests are made. It effectively protects citizen privacy while providing law enforcement with reliable and verifiable access to recover stolen vehicles. The system achieves a 98% reduction in bandwidth usage compared to traditional continuous streaming models  Β© 2026 IEEE.
