AB  - Optimal energy management in networked microgrids uses the blockchain concept to ensure security in energy transactions. Each energy transaction in networked microgrids is assumed to be a block with a hash address. A new transaction is considered to be another block of chaincode with a new hash address which is chained to the previous blockβ€™s hash address. For each block, using the cryptographic salt method, a random hash is used to produce a unique hash address with SHA-256 algorithm. The crowdsourcing concept is being applied in the energy system to create new operational models to obtain a real-time energy management system. This chapter proposes a methodology for the evaluation of the trust value of different nodes in the system. The Bayesian framework using beta probability distribution is considered for trust value evaluation for adequate energy transactions among various nodes. The hash keys and timestamps have been generated using python programming. Β© 2023 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
