AB  - This paper introduces the Federated Learning-Empowered Blockchain-based Data Sharing Scheme (FLBC-DSS), a novel framework designed to enhance data security and efficiency in Industrial Internet of Things (IIoT) environments. By integrating federated learning with blockchain technology, FLBC-DSS addresses the critical challenges of data privacy and unauthorized access, promoting secure, decentralized data sharing across various industrial sectors. Utilizing zk-SNARKs, the scheme provides a mechanism for anonymous data verification without compromising data integrity. Performance evaluations conducted using Hyperledger Fabric and SecureBoost demonstrate significant improvements in prediction accuracy and computational efficiency compared to traditional approaches. The implementation of non-cooperative game theory further illustrates the economic benefits of FLBC-DSS, highlighting its potential to increase profitability through strategic data sharing. The results affirm the effectiveness of FLBC-DSS in leveraging advanced cryptographic and machine learning techniques to foster a secure, transparent, and efficient digital ecosystem for IIoT.  Β© 2024 IEEE.
