AB  - This paper discusses the application of IoT-devices with low energy consumption and high-performance computing capabilities, for processing blockchain data using Neo Virtual Machine (NeoVM). NeoVM is a turing-complete computing machine, designed for Neo Blockchain, specially designed for cryptographic and deterministic (verifiable) computation. A NeoVM program is called a NVM Script (or just Script), and it is often used together with Neo Blockchain application capabilities, being called a Smart Contract. Smart Contracts are already used on other blockchains such as Bitcoin (although not Turing-complete) for value transfers, through the availability of verifiable information, i.e., transactions and transaction blocks, on a global ledger. However, due to the high processing costs and low throughput capabilities of global public chains, most industrial applications of blockchain require the usage of private/permissioned chains, with the goal of providing high-speed and low-cost information persistance. This work proposes an IoT device prototype capable of delivering blockchain private access to home applications (also called a Smart Home), in a new concept defined as Home Ledger. Applications of Home Ledger include: local permissioned access to sensors and home devices (through state-of-the-art cryptography); guaranteed verification of local stored data (through redundancy and byzantine fault tolerance consensus mechanisms); lowcost and high-performance local registry (through usage of lowenergy microcontrollers); auditable cameras and local security on Home Ledger; global availability by interfacing with a global public ledger. Β© 2019 IEEE.
