AB  - The rapid increase in digital data necessitates advanced storage solutions. This paper introduces the DNA-chain system, an innovative integration of DNA data storage and blockchain technology. Our hybrid system utilizes the high-density storage capability of synthetic DNA to handle massive amounts of data, alongside blockchainβ€™s robust security and traceability features. We detail techniques for encoding digital data into DNA sequences, addressing compression, redundancy, and error correction. Multi-layered encoding organizes data efficiently, while Optimized Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) processes facilitate swift data replication and retrieval. Live-Data Mutation Checks ensure data integrity against natural alterations, and Self-evolving Blockchain technology continuously adapts to new security challenges, enhancing protection against tampering. The system leverages DNAβ€™s parallel processing abilities, enabling multiple simultaneous data accesses, which improves throughput. DNA Digital Twins and Genetic Smart Markers mimic natural redundancy, enhancing retrieval efficiency. Real-time genetic analysis provides instant insights from stored data, supporting applications like long-term archival and time capsules. The DNA-chain system combines biological science with cryptographic techniques, offering a revolutionary, secure, and efficient data storage paradigm suited for future challenges. Β© The Institution of Engineering & Technology 2024.
