AB  - The technology known as blockchain has gained significant traction as the foundational infrastructure supporting the digital currency known as Bitcoin. Nevertheless, the advantages of this technology extend beyond its role in facilitating cryptocurrencies. Blockchain is a digital ledger that enables the recording of transactions between multiple parties in real time. It functions as a decentralized database where each participant maintains an identical copy of the ledger. The attractiveness of blockchain technology lies in its decentralized peer-to-peer network architecture, coupled with its cryptographic functionalities. The integration of this amalgamation empowers users to carry out transactions in the absence of a reliable third-party intermediary. According to (Alarcon and NG in Pennsylvania CPA J, 26β€“29, 2018), the potential advantages of blockchain technology in the field of accounting are particularly noteworthy. This is due to the fact that blockchain can facilitate a triple-entry accounting system, wherein all transactions are recorded in real-time, encrypted, and immutable with a time stamp. The objective of this Project is to conduct a comprehensive examination of existing literature pertaining to blockchain technology and evaluate its influence on the field of auditing. Β© The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd 2023.
