AB  - Blockchain technology is decentralized and immutable and offers several advantages for land registration Blockchain provides a transparent and tamper-resistant platform for verifying land transactions. Smart contracts eliminate the need for intermediaries and also reduce costs. This paper examines the key features and benefits of blockchain in land registration. Cryptographic signatures and timestamps further enhance the security of land records stored in blockchain. Overall, this paper demonstrates the transformative potential of blockchain technology in the realm of land registration. It provides valuable insights for land administration professionals, and technologists seeking to leverage blockchain for creating more efficient and trustworthy land registration systems, ultimately benefiting societies by safeguarding property rights and fostering economic development. Β© The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Singapore Pte Ltd. 2024.
