AD  - R. V. College of EngineeringΒ®, Department of Ise, Bengaluru, India
AB  - Blockchain technology has revolutionized various industries, introducing trust, transparency, and immutability to digital transactions. Notarization, a vital process for validating and authenticating documents and data, has also witnessed transformative advancements with blockchain integration. This paper presents a novel approach to notarization through blockchain, leveraging its inherent features to enhance security, efficiency, and accessibility. In this proposed system, each notarized document or data is represented as a distinct NFT, with its ownership and authenticity recorded on a decentralized blockchain network. The decentralized nature of the blockchain ensures consensus and eliminates single points of failure, while the NFTs digital fingerprint guarantees tamper-proof verification. Utilizing smart contracts, the NFTs embed essential metadata, including timestamps, cryptographic signatures, and relevant information about the notarized content. This design ensures the immutability of the notarization process, providing an indisputable trail of ownership and provenance. Integrating NFTs in notarization offers a revolutionary approach to secure, transparent, and efficient validation of documents and data. By harnessing the power of blockchain and NFTs, this technology paves the way for a new era of trust in digital transactions, making traditional notarization methods obsolete in an increasingly interconnected world.  Β© 2024 IEEE.
